    "description": "Alam Kuh is a high peak of the Takht-e Soleyman massif in northern Iran’s Alborz Mountains. Its granite climbing terrain and neighboring glaciers connect the mountain’s sporting history with the study of Iran’s high-altitude environment.",
    "tags": ["Alam Kuh", "Alborz", "Glaciers", "Mountaineering", "Mountain research"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "ready_for_review",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
